test(deploy): replace the host-timer test with the service it became (#237)

OPS-035 installed a host scheduler and read the unit back. There is no host
scheduler, so the test forked a script that no longer exists and took
`test (race)` and `coverage floors` down with it.

OPS-047 asserts the shape that replaced it, from the repository: the scheduler
script is gone, the Makefile installs no timer, the deployment declares a
backup service, and neither that service nor the script it runs names a
container-runtime socket. That last part is OPS-044's static half, and it is
the one that fails a pull request — which is where a socket would be added.

The behaviour of the service is elsewhere and stays there: its verdicts and its
window are scripts/backup-service-selftest.sh, which needs no Docker, and
OPS-045 is the live half.

It was mutation-tested by mounting a socket on the service, which turns the
gate red and names both spellings it finds.

